v1.2
- Fix: services/wifi-ap/run carried a UTF-8 BOM, so the kernel did not see a
  valid shebang and runsv could not exec it. Combined with "sleep infinity"
  (a GNU extension BusyBox sleep rejects), the no-op service was restarted
  once a second forever.
- Fix: removed services/wifi-ap/finish. It dated from v1, when this service
  owned the AP. Since v2 the AP belongs to /service/hostapd, but finish still
  deleted ap0, killed dnsmasq and removed the NAT rules on every stop of the
  no-op service - tearing down a live AP owned by another service. setup now
  deletes it from installs that already have it.
- Fix: clamp TCP MSS to the path MTU on the upstream interface. A cellular
  upstream is typically MTU 1450; without this, clients hit PMTU black holes
  where small requests work and larger responses never arrive.
- Improvement: MASQUERADE is now scoped to the AP subnet instead of every
  packet leaving the upstream interface. The old unscoped rule is deleted on
  start and on uninstall, so upgrading leaves no duplicate.
- Improvement: default DHCP lease raised from 2m to 12h. Existing
  wifi-ap.conf files are preserved and keep their current value.
- Cleanup: repaired mojibake in the hostapd template comments.

v1.1
- Fix: detect hostapd binary explicitly in service run script (/usr/sbin, /usr/bin, PATH)
- Fix: clear error message when hostapd is missing, with install hint
- Fix: cleanup FORWARD iptables rules on ap0 (not wlan0) in finish script
- Fix: stop dnsmasq-ap0 and remove ap0 virtual interface during service stop
- Improvement: setup now attempts to auto-install hostapd via opkg when missing

v1.0
- Initial release
- WiFi AP on ap0 virtual interface (BCM43438 / RPi3)
- Custom SSID + WPA2-PSK via wifi-ap.conf
- dnsmasq DHCP for clients (192.168.0.100-200)
- iptables NAT: ap0 -> wwan0 (4G internet sharing)
- Disables connman tethering (conflict with ap0)
- Compatible SetupHelper (install/uninstall/reinstall)
